  "redditGuideStep1": "Open reddit.com/prefs/apps with the button below. It opens inside Fern, so you are already signed in.",
  "redditGuideStep2": "Scroll to the bottom and press \"create another app...\" (or \"are you a developer? create an app...\").",
  "redditGuideStep3": "Pick the type \"script\". This is the one that gets missed: with any other type Reddit still creates the app, and then rejects every request without saying why.",
  "redditGuideStep4": "Give it any name you like, leave the description empty, and paste this into \"redirect uri\":",
  "redditGuideStep5": "Press \"create app\". Reddit shows you the card for the app you just made.",
  "redditGuideStep6": "The client ID is the short string right under \"personal use script\", at the top left of the card. The secret is the field labelled \"secret\".",
  "redditGuideStep7": "Come back here and paste both, plus your Reddit username and password.",
  "redditGuideTwoFactor": "With two-factor authentication on, write the password as password:code — Reddit expects both in the same field.",
  "redditGuidePrivacy": "The four values stay on this computer, encrypted, and are only ever sent to Reddit.",
  "redditGuideOpen": "Open Reddit",
  "redditGuideCopy": "Copy the redirect URI",
  "redditGuideCopied": "Redirect URI copied",

