  "danbooruTitle": "Danbooru",
  "danbooruDescription": "Fern downloads the posts you have favourited on Danbooru. Its API is public: all it needs is your account name and an API key.",
  "danbooruUsername": "Account name",
  "danbooruUsernameHint": "Your Danbooru user name",
  "danbooruApiKey": "API key",
  "danbooruApiKeyHint": "A key from your Danbooru profile",
  "danbooruApiKeyNote": "On Danbooru, open your profile, go to API Key and create one. It is not your password: you can revoke it whenever you like without changing anything else. It stays on this computer and is only used to talk to Danbooru.",

  "gelbooruTitle": "Gelbooru",
  "gelbooruDescription": "Fern downloads the posts you have favourited on Gelbooru. Its favourites API is slower than the rest: it hands out references rather than posts, so each one has to be asked for separately.",
  "gelbooruUserId": "Account id",
  "gelbooruUserIdHint": "The number of your Gelbooru account",
  "gelbooruApiKey": "API key",
  "gelbooruApiKeyHint": "The key of that account",
  "gelbooruApiKeyNote": "On Gelbooru, go to My Account, then Options, and look for API Access Credentials: both the id and the key are there. They stay on this computer and are only used to talk to Gelbooru.",

  "pinterestTitle": "Pinterest",
  "pinterestDescription": "Fern downloads what you have saved on Pinterest. Whatever is in public boards needs nothing but your account name.",
  "pinterestUsername": "Account name",
  "pinterestUsernameHint": "Your Pinterest user name",
  "pinterestSecretBoardsNote": "To bring in what you keep in secret boards, log in to Pinterest from Fern’s browser and press the key button there: the session is saved along with the name.",

  "pawchiveTitle": "Pawchive",
  "pawchiveDescription": "Fern downloads the posts you have favourited on Pawchive. There is nothing to fill in here: log in from Fern’s browser and press the key button there, and the session is saved.",

  "sourceGuideOpenSite": "Open the site",
  "sourceGuideOpenLogin": "Open the sign-in page",
  "sourceGuidePrivacy": "What you paste stays on this computer, encrypted, and is only ever sent to that site.",
  "sessionGuideStep1": "Press the button below. Fern opens the site in its own browser and takes you to the sign-in page.",
  "sessionGuideStep2": "Sign in exactly as you would anywhere else — captcha, email code and all. That is precisely why this cannot be done from outside.",
  "sessionGuideStep3": "Once you are in, press the key icon in the browser toolbar to save the session. Without this step nothing is saved and the import will still say it is not set up.",
  "sessionGuideExpires": "Sessions expire on their own after a while. When that happens Fern tells you, and repeating these steps is all it takes.",
  "danbooruGuideTitle": "Connecting Fern to Danbooru",
  "danbooruGuideIntro": "Danbooru gives every account an API key so programs can read on its behalf. You take it from your profile; your password is never involved.",
  "danbooruGuideStep1": "Open your profile with the button below and make sure you are signed in.",
  "danbooruGuideStep2": "Find the \"API Key\" row on your profile and press \"view\". Danbooru asks for your password to show it.",
  "danbooruGuideStep3": "If there is none yet, press \"Add\" and give it any name. One key is enough for Fern.",
  "danbooruGuideStep4": "Copy the long string it shows you.",
  "danbooruGuideStep5": "Come back here: the username is the same one you sign in with, and the key goes in the second field — not your password. Danbooru accepts it and simply returns nothing.",
  "danbooruGuideNote": "Revoking the key from that same page cuts Fern off immediately, without touching your password.",
  "gelbooruGuideTitle": "Connecting Fern to Gelbooru",
  "gelbooruGuideIntro": "Gelbooru hands you both values at once, written as a single line. Splitting that line in two is the whole job.",
  "gelbooruGuideStep1": "Open your account options with the button below and make sure you are signed in.",
  "gelbooruGuideStep2": "Scroll down to \"API Access Credentials\" and open the link it offers.",
  "gelbooruGuideStep3": "Gelbooru shows one line that looks like &api_key=abc123&user_id=456.",
  "gelbooruGuideStep4": "That line holds two separate values. Do not paste it whole into one field: Gelbooru accepts it and then nothing works, without saying why.",
  "gelbooruGuideStep5": "Put what comes after user_id= in the first field, and what comes after api_key= in the second.",
  "pixivGuideTitle": "Connecting Fern to Pixiv",
  "pixivGuideIntro": "Pixiv has no keys to copy. There is nothing to type here: you sign in inside Fern and the session is what identifies you.",
  "pixivGuideStep4": "That is it. Nothing to paste here — go to the import screen and pick Pixiv.",
  "pinterestGuideTitle": "Connecting Fern to Pinterest",
  "pinterestGuideIntro": "Your username alone is enough for public boards. The session is only needed for the secret ones.",
  "pinterestGuideStep1": "Type your Pinterest username in the field above. With that, public boards already work.",
  "pinterestGuideStep2": "Only if you also want the secret boards, press the button below and sign in.",
  "pawchiveGuideTitle": "Connecting Fern to Pawchive",
  "pawchiveGuideIntro": "There are no keys here either: you sign in inside Fern and the session is what identifies you.",
  "pawchiveGuideStep4": "Back here, choose below whether to bring your saved posts or everything from the creators you follow.",
  "pawchiveGuideLinks": "Posts often link to download sites (Mega, Drive, Pixeldrain). Fern brings in whatever it can on its own and lists the rest once the import ends.",

