  "settingsHelp": "Help",
  "tutorialSectionTitle": "Guided tour",
  "tutorialSectionNote": "A walk through the screens of the app and what each one is for. You can leave it at any point.",
  "tutorialOfferTitle": "Shall I show you around?",
  "tutorialOfferBody": "It is a short guided tour and you can leave at any point. If you would rather look around on your own, it is in the settings.",
  "tutorialOfferAccept": "Start",
  "tutorialOfferDecline": "Not now",
  "tutorialProgress": "{position} of {total}",
  "@tutorialProgress": {"placeholders": {"position": {"type": "int"}, "total": {"type": "int"}}},
  "tutorialSkip": "Leave",
  "tutorialBack": "Back",
  "tutorialNext": "Next",
  "tutorialDone": "Done",
  "tutorialWelcomeTitle": "Welcome to FeRN",
  "tutorialWelcomeBody": "A quick tour of what the app does. Move on with Next or the arrow keys, and leave with Escape.",
  "tutorialSidebarTitle": "This is how you move around",
  "tutorialSidebarBody": "Every screen lives here: your library, what you bring in from elsewhere, your favourites and the managers. The button above folds it away to give the content more room.",
  "tutorialImportTitle": "This is where content comes in",
  "tutorialImportBody": "Bring content from a remote source or from a folder on your disk. What arrives waits for review until you accept it, so nothing reaches the library without you seeing it.",
  "tutorialContentTitle": "Everything shows up here",
  "tutorialContentBody": "Your library. A click opens the viewer, right-click brings up the actions, and you can mark several at once to handle them together.",
  "tutorialTagsTitle": "Tag by dragging",
  "tutorialTagsBody": "The tags in the menu are also places to drop things: drag one or more items onto a tag and they are tagged. Click it and the library shows only what is in it.",
  "tutorialCreateTitle": "Creators, tags and fernies",
  "tutorialCreateBody": "Everything you organise with is created here: creators, tags, and fernies, which are the faces the app learns to recognise.",
  "tutorialSearchTitle": "Search",
  "tutorialSearchBody": "Search by name, creator or tag from any screen.",
  "tutorialSettingsTitle": "Everything else lives here",
  "tutorialSettingsBody": "Language, theme, folders, remote sources and recognition. This tutorial too, in case you want to see it again.",

  "tourGeneralTitle": "General tour",
  "tourGeneralDescription": "Where everything is and how content gets in. This is the one offered the first time.",
  "tourImportingTitle": "Bringing in and reviewing content",
  "tourImportingDescription": "Where content comes from, how it is reviewed, and what it takes for it to reach the library.",
  "tourImporting1Title": "From where, and how much",
  "tourImporting1Body": "Pick the source — a remote one or a folder on this computer — choose everything or only what is new since last time, and press Fetch.",
  "tourImporting2Title": "What arrives is reviewed here",
  "tourImporting2Body": "None of this is in your library yet. This grid is the inbox: what has been fetched, waiting for you to say what to do with it.",
  "tourImporting3Title": "Open one and decide",
  "tourImporting3Body": "A click opens it in the viewer. There you save it, which makes it final, or discard it: discarding takes it out of the database and asks whether to delete the file too.",
  "tourImporting4Title": "Its details, without leaving the viewer",
  "tourImporting4Body": "The information panel is where you set creator, tags, title and links. You edit it while looking at it, which is when you know what it is.",
  "tourImporting5Title": "And then it is in Content",
  "tourImporting5Body": "What you saved leaves the import grid and shows up in the library.",
  "tourManagersTitle": "Creators and tags",
  "tourManagersDescription": "The two ways of ordering what you have, and the quick way to tag several things at once.",
  "tourManagers1Title": "The list of creators",
  "tourManagers1Body": "Every creator you have. Pick one and the screen fills with their work.",
  "tourManagers2Title": "Their details",
  "tourManagers2Body": "Name, avatar and the links to their sites. What you change here is saved on the creator.",
  "tourManagers3Title": "Everything of theirs",
  "tourManagers3Body": "The content you have assigned to them, in a grid like the library one.",
  "tourManagers4Title": "Tags work the same way",
  "tourManagers4Body": "With one difference: a tag can hang from another, so they can be arranged as a tree.",
  "tourManagers5Title": "And you apply them by dragging",
  "tourManagers5Body": "From the library, drag one or more items onto a tag in the menu. It is the quick way to tag several at once.",
  "tourFernieTitle": "Fernie mode",
  "tourFernieDescription": "What a fernie is, where its examples come from, and how you mark them in the viewer.",
  "tourFernie1Title": "What a fernie is",
  "tourFernie1Body": "A face, a character or an object you want Fern to learn to recognise in your content.",
  "tourFernie2Title": "Here are yours",
  "tourFernie2Body": "Each fernie can propose a tag or a creator when it is found. With nothing linked it only trains: on its own it tags nothing.",
  "tourFernie3Title": "Its regions",
  "tourFernie3Body": "Each crop is an example of it, and those examples are what a model learns from. The more and the more varied, the better: with little variety it will learn the background instead of the fernie.",
  "tourFernie4Title": "You mark them in the viewer",
  "tourFernie4Body": "Open something, go into fernie mode and drag over what you want to mark. Hold the space bar or the middle button to move around the image.",
  "tourFernie5Title": "And then you train",
  "tourFernie5Body": "Fernies on their own recognise nothing. What recognises is a model trained with them.",
  "tourModelsTitle": "Models and recognition",
  "tourModels1Title": "Your models",
  "tourModels1Body": "A model is what actually recognises. You put it together from the fernies you give it.",
  "tourModels2Title": "Creating one",
  "tourModels2Body": "You pick its fernies and what it has to answer: whether each one is there or not, or which of them it found and where. The second needs at least two, because with one there is nothing to choose between.",
  "tourModels3Title": "Training takes a while",
  "tourModels3Body": "It runs in the background and you can keep using Fern meanwhile. The indicator in the top bar says how far along it is.",
  "tourModels4Title": "Recognising",
  "tourModels4Body": "A trained model goes over whatever content you point it at and proposes what it sees. Below the confidence threshold it proposes nothing.",
  "tourModels5Title": "Nothing is applied on its own",
  "tourModels5Body": "What it sees stays a suggestion until you accept it. You can accept in one go every suggestion above a given confidence.",
  "tourDuplicatesTitle": "Repeated content",
  "tourDuplicatesDescription": "How repeats are found, how you decide which copy stays, and what makes two things count as the same.",
  "tourDuplicates1Title": "Finding repeats",
  "tourDuplicates1Body": "Press Scan now and Fern goes over the whole library working out a fingerprint for each item. The first time it can take a while.",
  "tourDuplicates2Title": "The groups",
  "tourDuplicates2Body": "Each group is copies alike enough to be the same thing. The ones you have already answered do not come back.",
  "tourDuplicates3Title": "You decide which one stays",
  "tourDuplicates3Body": "Pick the copy you keep and the rest are discarded. You can merge into the one that stays the tags, creator, favourite and description of the discarded ones.",
  "tourDuplicates4Title": "The threshold, in Settings",
  "tourDuplicates4Body": "How different two items can be and still count as the same. Raising it groups more and starts joining things that merely look alike; lowering it leaves repeats unfound.",
  "tourDuplicates5Title": "And it looks on its own",
  "tourDuplicates5Body": "Every so often Fern goes over the library by itself and tells you if it finds anything. That period is in Settings too.",

  "tourModelsDescription": "How a model is put together, how long training takes, what happens to what it proposes, and how the tree decides which ones run.",
  "tourModels6Title": "The model tree",
  "tourModels6Body": "A model that is not in the tree never runs when recognising. The tree is what says which ones run, and in what order.",
  "tourModels7Title": "Putting them in and hanging them",
  "tourModels7Body": "The panel on the right holds the models that are outside. Pick a node in the tree and whatever you add hangs from it. A model cannot hang from itself or close a loop: the tree would bite its own tail.",
